{
  "_README": [
    "Model sources and hotspot positions for every machine that loads a real 3D model.",
    "",
    "Coordinates are in NORMALISED MODEL UNITS, not scene units. Every model is rescaled",
    "so its largest dimension is 1.0, centred on x and z, with its base sitting at y = 0.",
    "So y = 0.5 is half the model's height, whatever the model's real size.",
    "",
    "Each spot is [x, y, z, viewAngleDeg]:",
    "  x  left (-) to right (+)",
    "  y  base (0) to top of the model",
    "  z  back (-) to front (+)",
    "  viewAngleDeg  where the camera swings to when the part is selected, 0 = front",
    "",
    "'scale' converts normalised units to scene units, i.e. how big the machine appears.",
    "'parts' is only set for machines with a step-by-step teardown; the rest are one piece",
    "with hotspots.",
    "",
    "Run scripts/propose-hotspots.py to get measured starting coordinates for a new model,",
    "and scripts/qa.js to check that every spot still lands on the mesh."
  ],

